---
// The BeltManager half of every export guide. Checked against the live import (app #353, #373, #380) on 6 Nov 2026.
interface Props {
  locale: 'us' | 'uk';
}
const { locale } = Astro.props;
const us = locale === 'us';
const school = us ? 'school' : 'club';
---
<h2>Import the file into BeltManager</h2>
<p>
  BeltManager has one import for every system, so these steps are the same whichever tool your file came from.
  We last checked them against the live import on {us ? 'November 6, 2026' : '6 November 2026'}.
</p>
<ol>
  <li>Sign in as the {school} owner, go to <strong>Students</strong> and select <strong>Import</strong>.</li>
  <li>Select <strong>Choose CSV file</strong> and pick your file. It can hold up to 1,000 students and be up to 2 MB.</li>
  <li>
    Under <strong>Match your columns</strong>, check each column. BeltManager guesses from the headings. First name, last name
    and date of birth are required. You can also bring email, phone, guardian name, email and phone, group, current belt,
    status, medical notes and emergency contact. Set anything else to <strong>Don’t import</strong>.
  </li>
  <li>Select <strong>Check file</strong>. Each row is marked Add, Update, Skip or Error. Nothing is saved at this point.</li>
  <li>
    Fix any rows marked Error in your spreadsheet, then upload it again. Nothing can be imported until every row is clear.
  </li>
  <li>Select the <strong>Import</strong> button, which shows how many students will come in. You can undo an import for 24 hours if nothing has been recorded against those students since.</li>
</ol>

<h3>What usually needs fixing</h3>
<ul>
  {us ? (
    <>
      <li>
        <strong>Dates of birth.</strong> Change them to YYYY-MM-DD, such as 2016-03-14, before you import. BeltManager reads dates
        with slashes as day first. That means 03/14/2016 is rejected, and <strong>03/04/2016 is accepted as April 3, not March 4</strong>,
        with no warning.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Phone numbers.</strong> A US number has to include the country code, such as +15550123456. Without it the row
        is rejected with a message asking for a UK mobile number. If your numbers aren't in that form, set the phone columns to <strong>Don’t import</strong>
        and add them later. In Excel, format the column as Text first so it keeps the plus sign.
      </li>
    </>
  ) : (
    <>
      <li><strong>Dates of birth.</strong> Use DD/MM/YYYY, such as 14/03/2016.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Phone numbers.</strong> Only UK mobile numbers are accepted, starting 07 or +447. A row with a landline is rejected,
        so clear those cells or set the column to <strong>Don’t import</strong>.
      </li>
    </>
  )}
  <li>
    <strong>Status.</strong> The only accepted values are active and trial. Any other value, such as inactive, stops the file until you
    remove that row or set the column to <strong>Don’t import</strong>. Students with no status come in as active.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Under-18s.</strong> Every student under 18 needs a guardian in the file: a name, plus an email or a phone number.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Groups and belts.</strong> You don't need to set them up first. The import creates any group or belt it doesn't {us ? 'recognize' : 'recognise'}, and shows you the list first.
    New belts go at the end of the style's belt list, and you can reorder them in Settings.
    If your {school} teaches more than one style, write the belt as Style: Belt, such as Karate: Yellow.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Students already in BeltManager.</strong> A row with the same name and date of birth, or the same email, is skipped unless
    you tick <strong>Update students who are already in BeltManager</strong>.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Cards don't move in a CSV</h2>
<p>
  A CSV can't carry stored card details, so no card comes across in this import. Families re-add a card in BeltManager in April 2027,
  when card billing turns on. BeltManager is free until {us ? 'March 31, 2027' : '31 March 2027'}, so nobody needs a card on file before then.
</p>
